Openbox is a standards compliant, fast, light-weight, extensible
window manager.  Openbox was written first to comply with standards
and to work properly.  Openbox is fully functional as a stand-alone
working environment, or can be used as a drop-in replacement for
the default window manager in the GNOME or KDE desktop environments.

The package installs xinitrc examples in
/usr/doc/openbox-<version>/xinit/ and session helper scripts in
/usr/doc/openbox-<version>/.  Copy the files you need into
/etc/X11/xinit/ and /usr/bin/ if you want to start Openbox through
GNOME, KDE, or plain xinit.

Select "openbox-session" in xwmconfig, or "Openbox-Session" in a
display manager, if you want session management and your autostart
file to be used.
